/-!
# The actual plane-core group in the exchanged branch

The opposite cross-core movements identify the two intrinsic point cores
acting on the selected elementary plane. Applying the proved A.1.14 to
these literal cores constructs Y₀ = O₂(H) ∨ Qα. It induces all plane
automorphisms, its kernel is O₂(Y₀), and that kernel is generated by the
two fixed-core subgroups. The full plane normalizer normalizes Y₀.

The original-local application retains the selected critical path and
constructs the actual conjugation action and S₃ quotient. It also places
O₂(Y₀) in the two-core of the plane centralizer, the input to the subsequent
orthogonal centralizer estimate. No group-family label or assumed action
replaces the original cores or their conjugation maps.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, proof of 14.7.32, printed p.1058, applying
A.1.14, printed p.23, refs/quasithin.pdf. Construction of T_Y and Y and the
14.7.31 weak-closure contradiction remain subsequent source steps.
-/

public noncomputable section
open Subgroup Representation Representation.BinaryOffender
open scoped IsMulCommutative commutatorElement
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter14.Section07.LocalStructure.CriticalFusion.SourceConstruction.LocalReduction
